('India','india','Sri Lanka private tours for travelers from India, including short flights, family routes, Ramayana and Buddhist heritage, beaches, and long weekends.','India is Sri Lanka''s largest source market in SLTDA Jan-May 2026 data. Routes can be short, flexible, and family-friendly because flight access is strong.','Sri Lanka works well for Indian travelers because it combines close flight times, heritage, beaches, vegetarian-friendly food options, family travel, Ramayana trail interest, Buddhist heritage, and private chauffeur comfort.','Best fit: 5 to 8 days. Airport or Negombo, Sigiriya or Kandy, Nuwara Eliya or Ella, Galle or Bentota. Add Ramayana or Buddhist sites when requested.','Check visa rules, flight city, meal preferences, temple priorities, and whether the trip is a short break or full family holiday.','Year-round. South/west beaches are strongest November-April; east-coast beaches are stronger May-September.','[{"question":"How many days do Indian travelers need for Sri Lanka?","answer":"Five to eight days works for a focused route, while ten days gives better beach and hill-country pacing."}]','Plan Sri Lanka from India','Tell us your flight city, dates, and family needs. We will shape the route.',NULL,NULL,'Sri Lanka Tours from India','Plan private Sri Lanka tours from India with family routes, short breaks, Ramayana trail options, beaches, and chauffeur-guided travel.',NULL,1,1),
